(2146242, 294892, 15711, '<td valign="top">I studied this a long time.  Something draws me to it. It seems so simple and unaffected which I like.  The dark almost black of the red silo is appealing to me.  I wonder if it would be as effective with the barn cropped out, or perhaps shot from a different angle?  Well, anyway, if it evokes that much thought then it deserves at least a 7!! Good luck.</td>', 'I studied this a long time.  Something draws me to it. It seems so simple and unaffected which I like.  The dark almost black of the red silo is appealing to me.  I wonder if it would be as effective with the barn cropped out, or perhaps shot from a different angle?  Well, anyway, if it evokes that much thought then it deserves at least a 7!! Good luck.', '2006-02-13 01:31:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(2146245, 292639, 33352, '<td valign="top">Rule of thirds could have been better and given a stronger impact.....5</td>', 'Rule of thirds could have been better and given a stronger impact.....5', '2006-02-13 01:32:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(2146246, 294832, 15711, '<td valign="top">Almost like a skeleton, frozen in the snow.  I like what was once a trail that''s now covered with new snow and the new footprints in the upper right corner. The shadow of the metal adds a bit of extra texture to this simple image.  Upon second review, I''m bumping it up. 8</td>', 'Almost like a skeleton, frozen in the snow.  I like what was once a trail that''s now covered with new snow and the new footprints in the upper right corner. The shadow of the metal adds a bit of extra texture to this simple image.  Upon second review, I''m bumping it up. 8', '2006-02-13 01:32:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(2146251, 294727, 15711, '<td valign="top">I''m such a sucker for equine images.  I think with the tree, the hay bales and the fence lines, it would be a bit less busy if you cropped just past the horse on the right.  It would also make him a bit less centered and the overall image of him would be larger. Just a suggestion. Thanks for the smile!</td>', 'I''m such a sucker for equine images.  I think with the tree, the hay bales and the fence lines, it would be a bit less busy if you cropped just past the horse on the right.  It would also make him a bit less centered and the overall image of him would be larger. Just a suggestion. Thanks for the smile!', '2006-02-13 01:33:39.000000', NULL, 1),
